pdated_at":"2026-10-20T18:39:31Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2026-06-19T16:54:35Z"},"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-01-12T20:27:40Z","updated_at":"2026-04-23T13:41:29Z","closed_at":"2026-04-23T13:40:53Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in v4.5.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - Windows 10 - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1070\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using the Compatibility renderer, when either the width or height of a SubViewport is less than 41px, a CanvasGroup placed within it will turn completely black. See also #74622 \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nMake sure you are using Compatibility. Add a SubViewportContainer to the scene, to visualize the effect. Add a SubViewport that is 40px or less in width or height as a child of the SubViewportContainer. Add a CanvasGroup as a child of the SubViewport, and put something in the CanvasGroup as well (A Sprite2D or a ColorRect for example). Notice how the CanvasGroup turns black.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[px40_mrp_4.5.1.stable.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24572266/px40_mrp_4.5.1.stable.zip)\n\n<img width=\"1038\" height=\"587\" alt=\"Screenshot\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e9e8024c-238c-4ffe-a893-dfe94308edbc\" />","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.githu